From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyDevices <pydevices@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] webassembly: Take ticks from a monotonic clock.

mp_js_ticks_ms was Date.now() - MP_JS_EPOCH, so time.ticks_ms() followed
the host's wall clock. When that clock is stepped (an NTP correction, a
virtual machine syncing to its host, someone changing the time) the ticks
jump with it. A step back stalls every deadline computed from ticks_ms for
as long as the step, and audio that paces itself on ticks goes silent for
that long; a step forward makes every pending deadline fall due at once.
Under WSL 2 the clock steps back about 1.8 s every 32 s.

performance.now() is monotonic in browsers, in workers and in Node, so the
ticks come from it with the same epoch arithmetic. ticks_us was ticks_ms
times 1000; it now reads the same clock in microseconds, at whatever
resolution the host gives performance.now() (100 us or better in browsers).
"| 0" truncates and wraps both to the 32-bit value the C side expects, which
the ticks period then masks. time.time() keeps the wall clock.

diff --git a/ports/webassembly/library.h b/ports/webassembly/library.h
index 04b408d..13f3d11 100644
--- a/ports/webassembly/library.h
+++ b/ports/webassembly/library.h
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 extern void mp_js_write(const char *str, mp_uint_t len);
 extern int mp_js_ticks_ms(void);
+extern int mp_js_ticks_us(void);
 extern void mp_js_hook(void);
 extern double mp_js_time_ms(void);
 extern uint32_t mp_js_random_u32(void);
diff --git a/ports/webassembly/library.js b/ports/webassembly/library.js
index 0c38cce..ebac047 100644
--- a/ports/webassembly/library.js
+++ b/ports/webassembly/library.js
@@ -26,9 +26,16 @@
 
 mergeInto(LibraryManager.library, {
     // This string will be emitted directly into the output file by Emscripten.
-    mp_js_ticks_ms__postset: "var MP_JS_EPOCH = Date.now()",
+    // performance.now() is monotonic, unlike Date.now(), which follows every
+    // step of the host's wall clock (an NTP correction, a virtual machine
+    // syncing to its host) and would take the ticks with it.
+    mp_js_ticks_ms__postset: "var MP_JS_EPOCH = performance.now()",
 
-    mp_js_ticks_ms: () => Date.now() - MP_JS_EPOCH,
+    mp_js_ticks_ms: () => (performance.now() - MP_JS_EPOCH) | 0,
+
+    // The same clock in microseconds; "| 0" wraps it like the ticks it feeds.
+    mp_js_ticks_us__deps: ["mp_js_ticks_ms"],
+    mp_js_ticks_us: () => ((performance.now() - MP_JS_EPOCH) * 1000) | 0,
 
     mp_js_hook: () => {
         if (ENVIRONMENT_IS_NODE) {
diff --git a/ports/webassembly/mphalport.c b/ports/webassembly/mphalport.c
index 3935068..107ff5b 100644
--- a/ports/webassembly/mphalport.c
+++ b/ports/webassembly/mphalport.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ void mp_hal_delay_us(mp_uint_t us) {
 }
 
 mp_uint_t mp_hal_ticks_us(void) {
-    return mp_js_ticks_ms() * 1000;
+    return mp_js_ticks_us();
 }
 
 mp_uint_t mp_hal_ticks_ms(void) {
